{
 "schema": "katamari.hub-layout/3",
 "notes": "Hub-local Unity metres: origin HubCenter, +Y up, +Z north (left-handed). A board's readable side faces its local -Z; yawDeg turns it about +Y. Tools/hubart/build_hub_room.py builds the room model from this file: floor, walls, decor, each board's frame (size + frame margin), legs and bolts, and one Anchor_Board_<id> empty at the board's canvas plane (canvasDepthM in front of the board plane). The board panels themselves are the prefabs Assets/VRC_Katamari/Prefabs/Hub/HubBoard_<id>.prefab (Docs/Design/StoryMode/HUB_PANEL_PREFAB.md); Editor/Hub/HubAssembler.Room.cs instantiates them at the anchor pose (scale canvasMetresPerUnit) and wires them. Surfaces: the room's materials (one Art/Hub/Materials/<name>.mat each, built by the assembler with the shader below): colour (sRGB, multiplied over the texture), smoothness, and optionally a texture from 'textures' with the metres one copy of it covers (the model's UVs are in metres, so the material tiling is 1 / metresPerTile). Textures and sprites: import settings the assembler applies to each file under Art/Hub (sprite border = left, bottom, right, top in pixels).",
 "canvasMetresPerUnit": 0.001,
 "canvasDepthM": 0.06,
